<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
  <!-- ============================ WHICH MENU ENTRY IS WHICH PART OF THE PRODUCT
       Five of the nine entries on the left menu are whole missions that can be
       sold on their own. The other four — Home, Pay Run, People, Settings —
       deliberately carry NOTHING: a payroll product with no Pay Run is not a
       payroll product, and a switch nobody would ever flip is a switch that
       can only be flipped by mistake.

       WHY A FUNCTION AND NOT FIVE `record` LINES. Each entry belongs to the
       module that ships the mission (`pb_insights_hub`, `pb_mission`,
       `pb_learn`…), and this module depends on NONE of them on purpose — it is
       meant to be the cheapest thing on a customer's database. A `record` with
       a full XML id would make every one of those a hard dependency, and would
       fail outright on a database that has four of the five. The function
       below writes what it finds and says nothing about what it does not.

       It runs on install AND on every upgrade, which is what a correction here
       needs: an entry pointing at a feature key that no longer exists would
       otherwise stay pointed at it for ever, shown to everybody, with nothing
       on any screen to say so. -->

  <function model="pb.sidebar.item" name="_seed_feature_keys"/>
</odoo>
